Probe command:

```text
python.exe -u -c "import time; t=time.perf_counter(); import sklearn; print('sklearn', sklearn.__version__, 'seconds', round(time.perf_counter()-t,3)); from sklearn.ensemble import RandomForestClassifier; from sklearn.model_selection import RepeatedStratifiedKFold; print('RF_IMPORT_PASS')"
```

Observed output / failure:

```text
sklearn 1.9.0 seconds 6.237
ImportError: DLL load failed while importing _gradient_boosting: An Application Control policy has blocked this file.
```

A `RandomForestClassifier` cannot be imported because importing `sklearn.ensemble` imports the blocked compiled extension. Therefore Notebook 4 cannot faithfully execute in this environment. No fallback classifier, substituted implementation, changed parameters, or protocol workaround was used.

Additional probe: Python 3.14.6 (`C:\Python314\python.exe`) imported NumPy 2.5.3 and SciPy 1.18.1 but did not complete `import sklearn` within a 20-second bounded probe; it was not used for modelling. Python 3.13.2 lacks NumPy.

